00:00:29.400 --> 00:00:33.750
all part of the overall concept but the
book is really about there's these seven

00:00:33.750 --> 00:00:38.910
different elements that you want to make
sure your idea possesses so and those

00:00:38.910 --> 00:00:42.660
seven elements describe the problem at
the heart of the story so the problem

00:00:42.660 --> 00:00:45.960
has to be punishing and relatable and
original and believable and

00:00:45.960 --> 00:00:49.079
life-altering and entertaining and
meaningful those are the seventh acronym

00:00:49.079 --> 00:00:55.469
of problem so each one of those seven
things has to do with plot and character

00:00:55.469 --> 00:00:59.070
you know you want your characters to be
original in some way you want your

00:00:59.070 --> 00:01:02.340
plotting to be original in some way but
most importantly you want your concept

00:01:02.340 --> 00:01:06.470
to be original in some way the concept
that kind of holds it all together

00:01:06.470 --> 00:01:10.740
once you have an idea that meets all the
criteria that you've laid out in your

00:01:10.740 --> 00:01:14.640
book how do you go about structuring
that idea into a screenplay

00:01:14.640 --> 00:01:18.509
well a lot of people I mean I've worked
with clients as a coach you know

00:01:18.509 --> 00:01:22.350
consultant and help people do this and
help guide them through the process but

00:01:22.350 --> 00:01:27.330
I also do it myself as a writer and I do
think that the Save the Cat book [Author Blake Snyder] and its

00:01:27.330 --> 00:01:30.540
tools are helpful I mean I my favorite
thing about saving the cat really are

00:01:30.540 --> 00:01:36.420
the ten genres and working with and they
each have like five subgenres each that

00:01:36.420 --> 00:01:39.900
he goes into in the second save the cat
book save the cat goes to the movies

00:01:39.900 --> 00:01:44.430
those genres I think are super helpful
and very original and revolutionary for

00:01:44.430 --> 00:01:48.930
writers coming up with ideas for a movie
so I highly recommend those but he also

00:01:48.930 --> 00:01:52.170
has the beach heat which is the thing
that saved the cats most known for which

00:01:52.170 --> 00:01:57.030
is the 15 point structural paradigm
which I think was Blake Snyder building

00:01:57.030 --> 00:02:01.049
on other paradigms people had for 3x
structure going back to probably

00:02:01.049 --> 00:02:06.240
Aristotle but certainly Syd field and
other people's sense that and I think he

00:02:06.240 --> 00:02:09.959
